      "q": "11. In an Experiment $$\\mathbf{4}.\\mathbf{5}\\text{ }\\mathbf{kg}$$ of a fuel was completely burnt. The heat produced was measured to be $$\\mathbf{180},\\mathbf{000}\\text{ }\\mathbf{kJ}$$. Calculate the calorific value of the fuel.",
      "a": "The amount of heat released during combustion of $1\\text{ }kg$ fuel is known as calorific value i.e.,\n$Calorific\\text{ }Value=\\dfrac{Heat\\text{ produced during combustion}}{Quantity\\text{ of fuel}}$\n$\\Rightarrow Calorific\\text{ }Value=\\dfrac{180,000}{4.5}\\text{ }kJ/kg$\n$\\therefore Calorific\\text{ }Value=40,000\\text{ }kJ/kg$"
