      "q": "12. Can the Process of Rusting Be Called Combustion? Discuss.",
      "a": "A chemical process in which a substance reacts with oxygen to give off heat is called combustion. When an iron metal combines with the oxygen in the presence of water to form a compound\u00a0iron oxide is known as rusting.\nTherefore, the process of rusting can be called combustion because in both processes, heat, and light are produced. Rusting is known as slow combustion."
